"""Deterministic D3 textual corrections from recoverable D2 sources."""
from pathlib import Path
W=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
BASE=W/'planning/history/d2-candidate'
ROOT=Path(*W.parts[:W.parts.index('work')]) if 'work'in W.parts else None
# Archive paths preserve repository-relative names.
def source(rel):
 source_path=BASE/'work/nam-8227-nsscas-2026/workbench'/rel
 assert source_path.is_file(),source_path
 return source_path.read_text()
def change(rel,func):
 text=source(rel);text=func(text);(W/rel).write_text(text)
MISREAD="""**OD-6 / MR03 misread:** a genuine misread of question data, with object and difficulty unchanged, loses one earned A/B mark per datum in its first-use part. Deduct from the earliest earned A/B criterion in that part's listed order, never below zero; if none was earned, deduct zero and do not transfer the charge later. All eligible A/B awards then follow through on the misread data; judge M/DM normally and preserve www, dependency and OD-1 working requirements. Record the datum, canonical/misread values, first-use part, earned A/B, deducted criterion and prior deduction. Later parts do not charge that datum again. Own-figure errors and misreads making the task easier, changing its object/difficulty or leaving no solution use ordinary canonical marking. A named method error is not a data misread. Feedback names the misread. Authority: Vitalis OD-6; NSSCAS 2025 report PDF345 item4 (`CONVENTION:108`) says misreads cannot earn maximum marks; the one-mark allocation comes from **comparable Cambridge** `9709_m16_ms_12.pdf` PDF3, Penalties, adopted by Vitalis, and is not claimed as a Namibian tariff."""
old="Under the shared D2 misread rule, affected value-bearing B/A awards require the canonical givens; unaffected structural B and demonstrated M/DM can survive. Only an explicitly scoped official F.T. overrides this. For example, misreading a in the implicit curve can retain the structural remaining-y derivative G3 and genuine method G1/G4, but not canonical product accuracy G2 or final accuracy G5. Do not silently correct the input."
def shared(t):return t.replace('PLANNER Codex, 23 November 2026.','PLANNER Codex, 24 November 2026.').replace('**0.1.2**','**0.1.3**').replace('recipe-id@0.1.2:','recipe-id@0.1.3:').replace('D2 repairs D1;', 'D3 repairs D2;').replace(old,MISREAD)
def implicit(t):
 t=shared(t)
 t=t.replace('A valid explicit-quadratic method may demonstrate a different method path; full task credit is not a claim that every optional method facet was demonstrated. Store the demonstrated path rather than fabricating product-rule evidence.','Every accepted alternative route—explicit quadratic root, divided relation and log-absolute, as well as the product route—stores its actual demonstrated path. Full task credit does not establish every optional method facet. Do not fabricate product-rule evidence for a route that does not use that rule.')
 t=t.replace('A stated perpendicular-gradient value in working earns M1 without requiring an explicit reciprocal calculation.','A stated labelled perpendicular-gradient value **equal to −1/(their m)** in working earns M1 without requiring an explicit reciprocal calculation; negation or a positive reciprocal does not.')
 t=t.replace('including any justified identity/back-substitution needed by the route.','with no back-substitution allocated here. The justified root/y identity belongs in S3 only on the explicit-root route.')
 t=t.replace('S4: complete correct forward algebra reaches the given target','S4: complete correct forward algebra, including any required back-substitution, reaches the fixed given target')
 t=t.replace('An invalid logarithm of negative y is not accepted as this route.','At the supplied negative-y branch, writing $\\ln y$ without moduli is an invalid real relation: S1=0, dependent S2=0 and S4=0; independently correct remaining implicit derivative/constant evidence may earn S3=1, otherwise S3=0. Thus the maximum for that invalid route is **1/4**, not full proof credit. This is a proposed deterministic marking clarification (CALC-D2-DEV09 (D3 clarification)), pending confirmation and owner approval. The valid absolute-value route can earn4/4. A correct divided/log differentiation followed by failed or missing back-substitution earns **S1/S2/S3=3/4**, with S4=0; that step never costs S3 as well.')
 t=t.replace('although the separate H1/H2 application is judged on its own stated criteria.','the separate H1/H2 application earns **2/2** when its credible substitution gives the canonical value. H2 has no added www condition: the wrong-index error is already penalised in proof S2/S4. This known numerical coincidence is not OD-6 and does not restore proof marks or gradient-only G5.')
 t=t.replace('Current D2 checks are `planning/d2/calculus-design-check.py`, `calculus-domain-audit.json` and `calculus-exemplar-oracle.json`:', 'Current D3 checks are `planning/d3/calculus-design-check.py`, `calculus-domain-audit.json`, `calculus-exemplar-oracle.json` and `calculus-misread-oracle.json`:')
 # Explicit precedence prevents canonical accuracy language defeating OD-6.
 t=t.replace('Final canonical', 'Final canonical')
 t+='''\n## D3 per-part misread allocation and fixed proof target\n\nThe OD-6 exception qualifies ordinary canonical-only accuracy statements above. In criterion order the eligible A/B slots are: gradient-only **G2,G3,G5** (M: G1,G4); show-derivative **S2,S3,S4** (M: S1); extended gradient **H2** (M: H1); normal **N3** (M/DM: N1,N2). All eligible A/B slots can follow through, including structural B, with their required correct working. A previously charged datum incurs no further loss. If an eligible new datum first affects only the normal part, N3 is its only possible deduction; if N3 is not earned no deduction occurs.\n\nThe answer-given proof target is fixed. A misread that makes the curve and that target inconsistent changes the proof object and is ineligible for MR; use ordinary canonical marking. S4 never awards a proof of a changed target. Reading the actual target correctly and proving it later can earn its normal credit. This guard preserves MR09.\n\nExample, gradient-only normal case: genuinely read exponent coefficient k=2 as3 throughout the curve, retaining a=3, C=4 and P=(0,−4). The point still lies on the misread curve and the same product/chain/implicit task remains. Correct work gives $9e^{3x}y+(3e^{3x}+2y)y'=0$, then $m=-36/5$. All five awards are eligible before MR; deduct G2 as the first earned A/B: **4/5**. This is different from changing the exponential index by an invalid differentiation rule.\n\nExtended example: a correct proof earns4/4; only on reading the displayed formula for part(b), the learner misreads its numerator coefficient6 as8. Substitution yields $m=-32/5$, followed by $m_\\perp=5/32$ and $y+4=(5/32)x$ with full working. Charge H2 once: part(b) **1/2**, normal part **3/3** by OD-6 follow-through, total **8/9**. The ledger records a first misread use in gradient, not in the correctly read proof. Bare answers, an invalid reciprocal, a wrong e-index derivative, own-figure copying errors or a point no longer lying on the curve do not receive this MR treatment.\n'''
 return t

def stationary(t):
 t=shared(t)
 t=t.replace('`8227:2020:M2:T1:O04:D02`, `8227:2020:M2:T1:O04:D04` factor-theorem/factorisation route','`8227:2020:M2:T1:O04:D02`, `8227:2020:M2:T1:O04:D04`, `8227:2020:M2:T1:O03:D01`, `8227:2020:M2:T1:O03:D03` factor-theorem/division/quotient route')
 t=t.replace('`M2:T1:O04:D02/D04` (PDF14/printed11)', '`M2:T1:O04:D02/D04` and polynomial division/quotient `M2:T1:O03:D01/D03` (PDF14/printed11)')
 t=t.replace('not three extra direct-assessment facets.', 'not extra direct-assessment facets. Polynomial division remains outside this pilot’s direct coverage; it is explicitly recorded only as this optional route prerequisite.')
 t=t.replace('Final canonical A awards do not F.T.', 'Final canonical A awards do not ordinarily F.T.; OD-6 eligible misread data is the explicit accuracy-follow-through exception.')
 t=t.replace('Current D2 checks are', 'Current D3 checks are').replace('`planning/d2/calculus-design-check.py`','`planning/d3/calculus-design-check.py`')
 t+='''\n## D3 per-part misread allocation\n\nThe eligible A/B slots, in order, are points **P2,P4** (M/DM P1,P3), nature **C2** (M C1), flat point **I1,I3** (M I2), and flat classification **I4,I6** (M I5). I4 is a B accuracy award for the actual two-sided derivative behaviour, and follows through under eligible OD-6 data; it is not an unaffected generic recollection mark. Each slot still requires its observed evidence/dependencies. Deduct once only in the first-use part; later parts using the same datum can earn all their eligible accuracy awards without another deduction.\n\nTwo-extrema normal example: the learner genuinely reads the printed constant +2 as+3 in $f=x^3-3x+2$. The same derivative/factorisation and two-extrema demand remain; correct work gives stationary points $(−1,5)$ and $(1,1)$ and the same maximum/minimum tests. All six awards are eligible; deduct P2 as the first earned A/B in points, yielding **3/4+2/2=5/6**. The later classification incurs no further deduction.\n\nFlat normal example: read the printed constant −3 as−2 in $f=x^3-3x^2+3x-3$. Correct differentiation, repeated-factor solving and substitution give $(1,−1)$, with positive first derivative on both sides and a justified stationary inflexion. All awards are eligible; deduct I1 as the first earned A/B in point, giving **2/3+3/3=5/6**. Even though the constant vanishes on differentiation, the MR penalty is deducted deterministically from the earliest earned A/B slot of this first-use part; it is not a claim that the differentiation was wrong. Feedback names the incorrectly read constant.\n'''
 return t

def exemplar(t,implicit=True):
 t=shared(t).replace('`planning/d1/calculus-exemplar-oracle.json`','`planning/d3/calculus-exemplar-oracle.json`').replace('`planning/d1/calculus-design-check.py`','`planning/d3/calculus-design-check.py`')
 t=t.replace('N1 M1 visible negative reciprocal','N1 M1 labelled perpendicular gradient equal to −1/(their m)')
 t=t.replace('N3 stays0 unless the canonical exact line is obtained.','N3 stays0 unless the canonical exact line is obtained, except for eligible OD-6 genuine question-data misreads under the once-per-datum rule.')
 if implicit:
  t=t.replace('The equivalent log-absolute route is also mapped, never an invalid $\\ln y$ at these negative y values.','A failed or missing back-substitution after correct differentiation earns S1/S2/S3=3/4 and S4=0. The equivalent log-absolute route is also mapped. At the supplied negative-y branch an invalid $\\ln y$ without moduli gives S1=0, dependent S2/S4=0; separately correct S3 evidence can earn1/4 at most (CALC-D2-DEV09 (D3 clarification)).')
  t=t.replace('A stated labelled perpendicular gradient $m_\\perp=5/24$ is sufficient N1 method evidence;', 'The known wrong-index derivative substituted in part(b) gives H1/H2=2/2 because its value is canonical at x=0; proof S2/S4 remain lost. A stated labelled perpendicular gradient $m_\\perp=5/24=-1/(−24/5)$ is sufficient N1 method evidence;')
  t+='''\n## D3 OD-6 misread samples\n\nUse the matching work order’s per-part MR policy and deduction ledger; this is Vitalis’s OD-6, supported by NSSCAS report2025 PDF345 item4 plus comparable Cambridge9709/12 March2016 scheme PDF3, not a Namibian one-mark tariff.\n\nGradient normal: read k=2 as3 from the question, then differentiate correctly to $9e^{3x}y+(3e^{3x}+2y)y'=0$. The point (0,−4) remains on the curve. Substitution gives $m=-36/5$. All G1–G5 meet their evidence on the misread data; MR−1 comes from first earned A/B G2: **4/5**. Feedback: “You read the exponent coefficient as3; the question gives2. Your differentiation and substitution are consistent with3.”\n\nExtended normal: prove the actual displayed derivative correctly (4/4), then misread its numerator6 as8 only when applying part(b). Correct substitution gives $m=-32/5$, and shown normal working gives $m_\\perp=5/32$, $y+4=(5/32)x$. Deduct H2 once in part(b), **1/2**; normal **3/3**, total **8/9**. No second charge and no repair of a failed proof by changing its supplied target. The first-use ledger identifies the later numerator misread separately from the correctly read proof.\n\nMisreading own calculated −24/5, changing data so the supplied point is off the curve, changing the proof target, or using an invalid e-index rule is not this eligible MR case. A correct number with wrong e-index working still cannot earn gradient-only G5 www. No earned A/B means zero MR deduction.\n'''
 else:
  t=t.replace("Whole Bloom is proposed3 for two-extrema and4 only for the uncued mixed-outcome classification branch, pending the short cross-vendor check and Vitalis's approval.","Whole Bloom is **Apply3 for both branches under OD-4**; changed D3 marking clarifications await Claude confirmation, then Vitalis’s final-manifest approval.")
  t=t.replace('visible factor-theorem route earns I2;', 'visible factor-theorem/division/quotient route (M2:T1:O04:D02/D04 and O03:D01/D03, prerequisites only) earns I2;')
  t+='''\n## D3 OD-6 misread samples\n\nUse the matching work order’s own P/C/I criteria and once-per-datum ledger. Source authority is Vitalis OD-6, NSSCAS2025 report PDF345 item4, and comparable Cambridge9709/12 March2016 scheme PDF3; the one-mark tariff is not attributed to NSSCAS.\n\nTwo-extrema normal: read constant+2 as+3. Correct work on $x^3-3x+3$ gives $f'=3(x-1)(x+1)$, points $(−1,5),(1,1)$, and second derivative values−6,+6, hence maximum/minimum. Before MR all six awards qualify; deduct P2 (first earned A/B in points), so **3/4+2/2=5/6**. No later charge in nature.\n\nFlat normal: read constant−3 as−2. Correct work gives $f'=3(x-1)^2$, stationary $(1,−1)$, positive derivative on both sides and justified stationary inflexion. Deduct I1 (first earned A/B in point) once, **2/3+3/3=5/6**. I4 remains earned from the actual sign evidence; the rule does not remove all value-bearing awards.\n\nA slip in the learner’s own figures, a changed degree making the task easier, or data leaving no stationary solution receives ordinary canonical marking. Without earned A/B, MR deducts nothing; without required working OD-1 still gives zero.\n'''
 return t
change('work-orders/WB8227-implicit-normal.md',implicit)
change('work-orders/WB8227-stationary-inflexion.md',stationary)
change('exemplars/WB8227-implicit-normal.md',exemplar)
change('exemplars/WB8227-stationary-inflexion.md',lambda t:exemplar(t,False))
t=source('planning/calculus-source-reads.md').replace('`planning/d1/calculus-exemplar-oracle.json`','`planning/d3/calculus-exemplar-oracle.json`').replace('`planning/d1/calculus-domain-audit.json`','`planning/d3/calculus-domain-audit.json`')
t+='''\n## D3 source and marking clarification — 24 November 2026\n\nThe current planner checks are `planning/d3/calculus-design-check.py` and its D3 domain, exemplar and misread receipts. D1/D2 records remain historical source-reading evidence. Syllabus PDF14/printed11 was viewed again: the optional quartic factor-theorem route also needs linear polynomial division and identification of its quotient/zero remainder (`8227:2020:M2:T1:O03:D01/D03`), explicitly prerequisites only. No direct polynomial-division coverage is added.\n\nOD-6 uses the shared D3 native-page read: NSSCAS report2025 PDF345/printed343 item4 (`CONVENTION:108`), plus comparable Cambridge `9709_m16_ms_12.pdf` PDF3 Penalties. The NSSCAS line only prohibits maximum credit after a genuine misread; the one-mark A/B deduction/follow-through convention is Cambridge’s, adopted by Vitalis. It is never described as a Namibian official tariff.\n\nD3 retains all owned domains and twelve paper cases. It clarifies S4-only back-substitution, stored method paths for every alternative, the existing H1/H2 numerical coincidence, the −1/(their m) normal condition and the proposed maximum1/4 for invalid ln(y) at the supplied negative branch. These are author-side stage-D checks, not independent acceptance, a runtime marker or release approval.\n'''
(W/'planning/calculus-source-reads.md').write_text(t)
